      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespace_marmot_1_1_testing_1ab53dc9b566332842d48381549aa8090a" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void Marmot::Testing::checkDescribingTheStiffnessLeavesTheParticleUnchanged</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;name, Marmot::Discretizations::Meshfree::Particle &amp;particle, const std::vector&lt; double &gt; &amp;stateVars, const Eigen::VectorXd &amp;dQ, bool explicitPath)</argsstring>
        <name>checkDescribingTheStiffnessLeavesTheParticleUnchanged</name>
        <qualifiedname>Marmot::Testing::checkDescribingTheStiffnessLeavesTheParticleUnchanged</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>name</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_meshfree_1_1_particle" kindref="compound">Marmot::Discretizations::Meshfree::Particle</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>particle</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::vector&lt; double &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>stateVars</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const Eigen::VectorXd &amp;</type>
          <declname>dQ</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>bool</type>
          <declname>explicitPath</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Check that a particle that describes its stiffness (Particle::describeStiffness()) is left as it was found, in the middle of an increment: advanced by <computeroutput>dQ</computeroutput> and not yet accepted, so that its state holds the increment and its material point keeps the response of it, both of which the zero increment of the description would overwrite. The state variables, the bound of two descriptions in a row (addBoundOfAbsoluteStiffnessTimes()) and, for a particle with the explicit path, the internal force before and after a description, which reads the response the material point keeps, must be equal to the last bit; also after a description whose visitor throws. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the particle, for the messages. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>particle</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The particle, with kernel functions assigned. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>stateVars</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Its state variables. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>dQ</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The increment of its nodes, node-wise. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>explicitPath</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether the particle has the explicit path: it is advanced by updatePhysicsExplicit() and its explicit internal force is compared; else it is advanced by computePhysicsKernels(). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::runtime_error</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>(throwExceptionOnFailure()) if the description changes the particle. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
